  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Summer-like conditions this week\n\n-  Chance for showers/thunderstorms in Lemhi County and southwest\n   Montana today\n\n-  Cold front Friday to bring a change: showers and thunderstorms,\n   gusty winds, then cooler, fall-like conditions this weekend.\n\n-  Frosty mornings to follow this weekend into early next week.\n\n\nLow pressure spinning over Nevada this morning will track\nnortheast today, sending moisture into Lemhi County and southwest\nMontana, including Butte, this afternoon and evening. There will\nbe enough moisture and instability to fuel showers and\nthunderstorms. Wind gusts to 30 mph and lightning will be the \nmain threats. Otherwise, expect fair weather across the Northern\nRockies featuring above-normal temperatures, light winds, and\nclear skies, through Thursday under dry southwesterly flow aloft.\n\nOn Friday, a cold front will disrupt our recent warm and dry \nweather. Despite timing differences with the front passage, there \nis a chance for showers and possibly thunderstorms if we're able \nto warm up enough. If we were to get a squall line forming with \nthe front with embedded thunder, then strong gusty winds could be \npossible impacting recreation on area lakes. \n\nOn Saturday, it could remain quite breezy across the region, but \nit will be much cooler with highs in the 60s. Some locations \nacross northwest Montana may remain showery with some cloud cover.\nThese areas could experience temperatures in the 50s until any \nsun breaks out. Both Saturday and Sunday temperatures will be near\nto below seasonal levels. With the colder night-time \ntemperatures, frost will again be in the cards.",
